 {:seon.task/name "the-test-service-runs-each-item-once-for-every-asker"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-11-10/11: \"I don't want 'shards' anymore. I want the flow system that is always only letting the tests run that we have cores for and is updating the db as they run so we can immediately return the results to agents\"; \"Never do timers if we can setup blocking channels\"; workers \"configurable via a config option\". Step 2 of the test system as a Flow (docs/merging.md#the-test-service; the design for the owner: notes test-system-as-a-flow-2026-11-10.md). Built on jolt/tests-items (c5d9322bb0, not landed): seon.prove/prove-proc holds many runs at once (one per key), each planned by the agent holding its branch (seon.agent/run-plan, answered for :tests with :plan?: the items to run at their digests, what it reuses and defers); the items, (test, digest) pairs, join one queue (seon.prove/ask-items): an item many runs need is queued once and run once, granted one at a time to a free worker (:seon.config.proofs/max-workers, default 8) as {:op :tests :names #{test}}, an agent's turn first, then by waiters and measured time, aged by skips; a run is answered at its first red item or its last green (seon.prove/batch-ended, settle, run-answer). seon.prove-test green (21; its proofs there: an-item-many-ask-runs-once-and-answers-each, a-red-answers-its-asker-at-once-and-drops-what-only-it-wanted, a-turns-item-goes-ahead-of-a-batchs, a-worker-pulls-one-item-at-a-time, a-batch-that-died-answers-its-askers-with-the-error; named here once they land). Left: (1) seon.agent-test/a-process-test-gets-its-verdict-while-the-agent-can-act is red: a process-test proof comes back :none (the answer has :deferred [] and reused 1 where the old path deferred it to the gate): find where the plan's :deferred is lost; (2) the worker is a fork of the agent per item (measured 2026-11-11: ~10 ms a fork from a 103 MB agent, flat at 1-1,000 items; 16-35 MB own per child, ~45 MB after a full collection, so the child runs its one test and exits with no full collection): grants still run in the agent's run-tests-forked; (3) a seon.cost proof that dispatch stays microseconds an item (grant scans the queue: O(queued) a grant); (4) branch facts written once per answered ask for an asker on another agent; (5) then sessions ask root (seon.root/a-session-is-a-branch-and-bin-prove-asks-root, Optimization's server op) and bin/prove stops sharding. Verdicts as store facts is the owner's open choice (the plan keeps the digest-keyed cache, docs/merging.md#verdicts-are-a-cache)."
